            "text_YkXPcC": {
              "type": "text",
              "name": "t:names.description",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Radical Transparency</strong><br/>Every product shows the exact dollars going to charity. We could be vague about it. We could say \"a portion of proceeds\" and technically be telling the truth. But that's what everyone else does and honestly it's a little sus. You deserve to see the number. So we show you the number.</p><p><strong>No Guilt Trips</strong><br/>We're not here to make you feel bad about shopping. That's a terrible business strategy and also just annoying. You're going to buy things. That's fine. That's normal. We just made it so your purchases actually do something beyond making a shipping label. Shop because you want to, not because we guilted you into it.</p><p><strong>Partnerships That Actually Work</strong><br/>Here's a secret about most brand-charity partnerships: the brand gets great PR and the charity gets a check that wouldn't cover a month of office rent. Our model is different. Brands keep their wholesale margins — we don't ask them to sacrifice anything. The charitable donation comes from our side. Which means the charities get real, meaningful funding. And the brands get to be part of something without it costing them a dime. Everyone wins except our profit margins, which are a work in progress.</p><p><strong>Products We'd Actually Buy</strong><br/>We don't carry random stuff just because it has a good margin. If we wouldn't buy it for ourselves, we're not putting it on the site. Every product here is something we genuinely think is good. We carry brands like Johnnie-O, Marine Layer, Outerknown, Herbivore Botanicals, and Homesick because they make things people actually want. This is a shopping destination first. The charity part makes it better, but the products have to be worth buying on their own.</p>",
                "width": "100%",
                "max_width": "none",
                "alignment": "left",
                "type_preset": "rte",
                "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                "font_size": "1rem",
